  "contracts": {
    "sines": "Private 1024 entries using binary32(360/1023), double pi and reciprocal 180; retail phase-offset table unchanged.",
    "vertices": "Unclamped binary32 weights, double packed-coordinate terms and origin move before final float store. Zero fraction ignores move. Same frames select zero.",
    "normals": "Native packed angle indices; retained double X and spilled binary32 Y products, then original double-length normalization only with a nonzero fraction.",
    "culling": "Normalized axes use one/equal-frame or two/different-frame sphere calls; matching IN/OUT decides. Otherwise merged old/new bounds expand by binary32(origin-oldorigin) for flag 0x40, independent of fraction/axes. Valid bounds also supplied to lighting/caster consumers.",
    "publication": "Frame/span/count checks before indexing; entire surface numeric staging before raster or ray vertex publication; unchanged published geometry on numeric failure. Float[4] fourth components remain untouched. Loader retains allocation ownership.",
    "profile_isolation": "Only q3-ihv entities submitted through the native entry point use these paths. Existing modern sine tables/interpolation retained. Obsolete post-interpolation move helper removed."
